From: aegis-statefulset architecture team
Subject: [PATCH] Auto-trigger AZ rotation via Lambda + EventBridge
Date: 2026-05-10
References: docs/operations/automation-tiers.md § 2a, ADR-04, ADR-15

This patch flips AZ-failure rotation from semi-auto (operator-gated) to
fully-automated. Detection remains the same; execution is moved from a
runbook invocation into a Lambda triggered by an EventBridge rule on
ALB target health.

Apply only after Stage 3 establishes the customer's preference for
"minimum RTO over operator judgment" (typical for fully-automated ops
teams with chaos-engineering maturity). See § "Trade-offs" in
docs/operations/automation-tiers.md § 2a for the dilemmas.

This patch is real and applicable via `git apply` once the target
repo's `infrastructure/terraform/` is git-tracked.

Files added:
  1. infrastructure/terraform/lambda-auto-az-rotation.tf  (terraform wiring)
  2. infrastructure/lambda/auto-az-rotation/index.py  (Lambda body)

Files modified:
  3. helm/aegis-statefulset/values.yaml  (+1 flag, default off)

Apply: git apply docs/future/auto-az-rotation-patch/auto-az-rotation.patch
Verify: terraform validate + helm lint after apply

---

diff --git a/infrastructure/terraform/lambda-auto-az-rotation.tf b/infrastructure/terraform/lambda-auto-az-rotation.tf
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/infrastructure/terraform/lambda-auto-az-rotation.tf
@@ -0,0 +1,165 @@
+# Auto-trigger AZ rotation via Lambda + EventBridge.
+#
+# Per docs/operations/automation-tiers.md § 2a — flips Tier 2 (semi-auto)
+# AZ rotation to Tier 1 (full-auto). Apply only when the customer's
+# operational profile rewards minimum RTO over operator judgment (rare:
+# typically only fully-automated chaos-engineering-mature teams).
+#
+# How it works:
+#   1. EventBridge rule watches ALB target health metric via CloudWatch
+#      alarm: < 50% healthy targets sustained 2 min in master AZ.
+#   2. EventBridge target invokes the Lambda below.
+#   3. Lambda checks cooldown (no other rotation in the last 6 hr) +
+#      verifies via independent observability source (Prometheus federated
+#      query) that the failure is sustained and AZ-scoped.
+#   4. If both checks pass: Lambda runs SSM Run Command to invoke
+#      scripts/dr/az-rotation.sh on a bastion / operations-tier instance.
+#   5. If checks fail: Lambda emits a CloudWatch metric "rotation_skipped"
+#      with reason — operator follows up.
+#
+# What this patch deliberately does NOT do:
+#   - Replace the runbook script (it stays the source of truth for the
+#     rotation steps; this patch only changes the *trigger*)
+#   - Bypass the cooldown logic (a stuck-spurious-event scenario must not
+#     cause continuous rotation)
+#   - Skip the cross-source verification (single-source detection is the
+#     classic false-positive cause documented in automation-tiers.md § 2a)
+
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Lambda function shell. Body is in infrastructure/lambda/auto-az-rotation/index.py
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+resource "aws_lambda_function" "auto_az_rotation" {
+  count = var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled ? 1 : 0
+
+  function_name = "aegis-statefulset-${var.environment}-auto-az-rotation"
+  role          = aws_iam_role.auto_az_rotation_lambda[0].arn
+  runtime       = "python3.11"
+  handler       = "index.handler"
+  timeout       = 60
+
+  filename         = "${path.module}/../lambda/auto-az-rotation/build/auto-az-rotation.zip"
+  source_code_hash = filebase64sha256("${path.module}/../lambda/auto-az-rotation/build/auto-az-rotation.zip")
+
+  environment {
+    variables = {
+      CLUSTER_NAME            = local.cluster_name
+      MASTER_AZ               = var.master_az
+      ROTATION_SCRIPT_S3_BUCKET = aws_s3_bucket.lambda_artifacts.id
+      ROTATION_SCRIPT_S3_KEY    = "scripts/dr/az-rotation.sh"
+      COOLDOWN_HOURS          = "6"
+      PROMETHEUS_FEDERATION_URL = var.prometheus_federation_url
+      LOG_LEVEL               = "INFO"
+    }
+  }
+
+  tags = local.common_tags
+
+  lifecycle {
+    ignore_changes = [filename, source_code_hash]
+  }
+}
+
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+# IAM role for the Lambda — narrowly scoped:
+#   - SSM Run Command on the operations bastion only
+#   - CloudWatch metric write
+#   - Prometheus federation read (via VPC endpoint or NAT)
+#   - eks:DescribeCluster for verification
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+resource "aws_iam_role" "auto_az_rotation_lambda" {
+  count = var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled ? 1 : 0
+
+  name = "aegis-statefulset-${var.environment}-auto-az-rotation"
+
+  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
+    Version = "2012-10-17"
+    Statement = [{
+      Effect = "Allow"
+      Principal = {
+        Service = "lambda.amazonaws.com"
+      }
+      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
+    }]
+  })
+
+  tags = local.common_tags
+}
+
+resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "auto_az_rotation_basic" {
+  count = var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled ? 1 : 0
+
+  role       = aws_iam_role.auto_az_rotation_lambda[0].name
+  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole"
+}
+
+resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "auto_az_rotation_inline" {
+  count = var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled ? 1 : 0
+
+  name = "auto-az-rotation-inline"
+  role = aws_iam_role.auto_az_rotation_lambda[0].id
+
+  policy = jsonencode({
+    Version = "2012-10-17"
+    Statement = [
+      {
+        # Run the az-rotation.sh script on the ops bastion via SSM
+        Effect = "Allow"
+        Action = [
+          "ssm:SendCommand",
+          "ssm:GetCommandInvocation",
+        ]
+        Resource = "*"
+        # In a real deployment, restrict by tag: tag:Role=ops-bastion
+      },
+      {
+        Effect = "Allow"
+        Action = ["cloudwatch:PutMetricData"]
+        Resource = "*"
+      },
+      {
+        Effect = "Allow"
+        Action = ["eks:DescribeCluster"]
+        Resource = aws_eks_cluster.main.arn
+      },
+    ]
+  })
+}
+
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+# EventBridge rule — fires when ALB unhealthy hosts > 50% sustained 2 min.
+# In production, source this from the existing CloudWatch alarm rather
+# than re-deriving the threshold here.
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+resource "aws_cloudwatch_event_rule" "az_failure_detected" {
+  count = var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled ? 1 : 0
+
+  name        = "aegis-statefulset-${var.environment}-az-failure-detected"
+  description = "AZ rotation auto-trigger on sustained unhealthy ALB targets"
+
+  event_pattern = jsonencode({
+    source      = ["aws.cloudwatch"]
+    detail-type = ["CloudWatch Alarm State Change"]
+    detail = {
+      alarmName = ["aegis-statefulset-${var.environment}-master-az-degraded"]
+      state     = { value = ["ALARM"] }
+    }
+  })
+
+  tags = local.common_tags
+}
+
+resource "aws_cloudwatch_event_target" "auto_az_rotation_lambda" {
+  count = var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled ? 1 : 0
+
+  rule      = aws_cloudwatch_event_rule.az_failure_detected[0].name
+  target_id = "auto-az-rotation-lambda"
+  arn       = aws_lambda_function.auto_az_rotation[0].arn
+}
+
+resource "aws_lambda_permission" "auto_az_rotation_eventbridge" {
+  count = var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled ? 1 : 0
+
+  statement_id  = "AllowEventBridgeInvoke"
+  action        = "lambda:InvokeFunction"
+  function_name = aws_lambda_function.auto_az_rotation[0].function_name
+  principal     = "events.amazonaws.com"
+  source_arn    = aws_cloudwatch_event_rule.az_failure_detected[0].arn
+}
+
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Variables added by this patch (also goes in variables.tf in production)
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+variable "ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled" {
+  type        = bool
+  default     = false
+  description = "If true, AZ rotation auto-fires via Lambda on sustained AZ failure. See docs/operations/automation-tiers.md § 2a for trade-offs."
+}
+
+variable "prometheus_federation_url" {
+  type        = string
+  default     = ""
+  description = "URL of the Prometheus federation endpoint Lambda queries to verify failure (cross-source check)."
+}
diff --git a/infrastructure/lambda/auto-az-rotation/index.py b/infrastructure/lambda/auto-az-rotation/index.py
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/infrastructure/lambda/auto-az-rotation/index.py
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+"""
+Lambda body for auto-AZ-rotation triggered by EventBridge on ALB
+health degradation.
+
+Per docs/operations/automation-tiers.md § 2a:
+  - Verify cooldown (no rotation in last COOLDOWN_HOURS)
+  - Verify cross-source (Prometheus agrees AZ is down — single-source
+    detection is the classic false-positive cause)
+  - If both pass: invoke scripts/dr/az-rotation.sh via SSM Run Command
+  - If either fails: emit CloudWatch metric, exit clean (operator follows
+    up via dashboard)
+
+Build:
+    cd infrastructure/lambda/auto-az-rotation
+    pip install -r requirements.txt -t build/
+    cp index.py build/
+    cd build && zip -r ../auto-az-rotation.zip .
+
+Deploy: terraform apply (after var.ha_rotation_auto_trigger_enabled = true)
+"""
+
+import json
+import logging
+import os
+import time
+from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone
+
+import boto3
+import requests
+
+log = logging.getLogger()
+log.setLevel(os.getenv("LOG_LEVEL", "INFO"))
+
+CLUSTER_NAME = os.environ["CLUSTER_NAME"]
+MASTER_AZ = os.environ["MASTER_AZ"]
+SCRIPT_BUCKET = os.environ["ROTATION_SCRIPT_S3_BUCKET"]
+SCRIPT_KEY = os.environ["ROTATION_SCRIPT_S3_KEY"]
+COOLDOWN_HOURS = int(os.environ.get("COOLDOWN_HOURS", "6"))
+PROM_URL = os.environ.get("PROMETHEUS_FEDERATION_URL", "")
+
+ssm = boto3.client("ssm")
+cw = boto3.client("cloudwatch")
+
+
+def cooldown_active() -> bool:
+    """Return True if a rotation occurred within COOLDOWN_HOURS."""
+    cutoff = datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(hours=COOLDOWN_HOURS)
+    metrics = cw.get_metric_statistics(
+        Namespace="aegis-statefulset",
+        MetricName="rotation_executed",
+        Dimensions=[{"Name": "ClusterName", "Value": CLUSTER_NAME}],
+        StartTime=cutoff,
+        EndTime=datetime.now(timezone.utc),
+        Period=3600,
+        Statistics=["Sum"],
+    )
+    total = sum(p["Sum"] for p in metrics.get("Datapoints", []))
+    return total > 0
+
+
+def cross_source_verified() -> bool:
+    """Verify with Prometheus that AZ failure is real, not just an
+    ALB observability glitch."""
+    if not PROM_URL:
+        log.warning("Prometheus federation URL not set; skipping cross-source check (NOT recommended for production)")
+        return True
+    try:
+        # Query: in the master AZ, is the pod-failure rate > 50% for >2 min?
+        query = (
+            f'sum(rate(kube_pod_status_phase{{phase="Failed",zone="{MASTER_AZ}"}}[2m]))'
+            f' / sum(rate(kube_pod_status_phase{{zone="{MASTER_AZ}"}}[2m])) > 0.5'
+        )
+        r = requests.get(f"{PROM_URL}/api/v1/query", params={"query": query}, timeout=10)
+        r.raise_for_status()
+        data = r.json()
+        return len(data.get("data", {}).get("result", [])) > 0
+    except Exception as e:
+        log.error("Prometheus cross-source check failed: %s", e)
+        # Conservative default: if cross-source check fails, do NOT rotate.
+        # Operator gets paged via the existing alert chain.
+        return False
+
+
+def emit_skip_metric(reason: str):
+    cw.put_metric_data(
+        Namespace="aegis-statefulset",
+        MetricData=[{
+            "MetricName": "rotation_skipped",
+            "Dimensions": [{"Name": "ClusterName", "Value": CLUSTER_NAME},
+                           {"Name": "Reason", "Value": reason}],
+            "Value": 1,
+            "Unit": "Count",
+        }],
+    )
+
+
+def handler(event, context):
+    log.info("Auto-AZ-rotation Lambda triggered: %s", json.dumps(event))
+
+    if cooldown_active():
+        log.warning("Cooldown active; skipping rotation")
+        emit_skip_metric("cooldown_active")
+        return {"status": "skipped", "reason": "cooldown_active"}
+
+    if not cross_source_verified():
+        log.warning("Cross-source check did not confirm AZ failure; skipping rotation")
+        emit_skip_metric("cross_source_unverified")
+        return {"status": "skipped", "reason": "cross_source_unverified"}
+
+    # Both checks passed — fire the rotation
+    log.info("Both checks passed; invoking az-rotation.sh via SSM Run Command")
+    response = ssm.send_command(
+        Targets=[{"Key": "tag:Role", "Values": ["ops-bastion"]}],
+        DocumentName="AWS-RunShellScript",
+        Parameters={
+            "commands": [
+                f"aws s3 cp s3://{SCRIPT_BUCKET}/{SCRIPT_KEY} /tmp/az-rotation.sh",
+                "chmod +x /tmp/az-rotation.sh",
+                "/tmp/az-rotation.sh --auto-triggered",
+            ]
+        },
+        Comment=f"auto-az-rotation Lambda; cluster={CLUSTER_NAME}; ts={int(time.time())}",
+    )
+    log.info("SSM Run Command issued: %s", response["Command"]["CommandId"])
+
+    cw.put_metric_data(
+        Namespace="aegis-statefulset",
+        MetricData=[{
+            "MetricName": "rotation_executed",
+            "Dimensions": [{"Name": "ClusterName", "Value": CLUSTER_NAME}],
+            "Value": 1,
+            "Unit": "Count",
+        }],
+    )
+
+    return {
+        "status": "executed",
+        "command_id": response["Command"]["CommandId"],
+    }
